    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a welcome notification emitted on the `NOTIFY` logger whenever an owner is successfully created.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `service/WelcomeNotifier.java`: a small, single-responsibility `@Component` that mirrors the existing `OwnerAuditLogger` pattern. It holds a `NOTIFY` logger and exposes `welcome(Owner)`, which emits a line carrying the owner's id and member id. Keeping this as its own component (rather than folding it into `OwnerAuditLogger`, whose job is the `AUDIT` trail) preserves clean separation \u2014 notification vs. audit are distinct responsibilities.\n\n**Wired into** `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the sole `POST /api/owners` handler): injected the `WelcomeNotifier` via the constructor and called `welcomeNotifier.welcome(owner)` right after the successful save/audit, on the create path only, so it fires exactly once per successful creation.\n\nResults:\n- New `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 a `NOTIFY` line contains both the owner id and the `memberId`.\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nObserved output confirms it: `INFO NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`.",
